session Path_Space_Operations = Continuous_Path_Spaces +
  description "
    Operations on laws of continuous paths that carry a state together with
    its running covariation.  Cutting, glueing, shifting, delaying and
    re-basing a path, each continuous and Borel measurable for the
    supremum metric, and the same operations on path laws: the law of a
    concrete process, glueing a law to a kernel of continuations chosen by
    the endpoint, and splitting a law at a stopping time and reassembling
    it by addition.  Stopping times as path functionals, the regular
    conditional distribution of the future given the stopped past, and
    optional sampling on the path space.  The martingale identities, and the
    closed clauses of a constraint on the covariation, pass through weak
    limits of laws.  The class of martingale laws whose covariation has its
    density in a given set of matrices, with its elementary properties, and
    the value function of the minimum-exit-time problem over that class,
    with the set of matrices and the domain as parameters.
  "
  options [document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  sessions
    Symmetric_Matrix_Spectra
    Disintegration
  theories
    Pair_Path_Space
    Pair_Path_Laws
    Path_Splicing
    Path_Stopping_Times
    Path_Law_Pasting
    Path_Law_Sampling
  theories [document = false]
    No_Viscosity_Ancestor
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
